prompts.template:
Here are the lyrics of a song called "{title}".

{role:lyrics}

Be specific and be hard on it: which lines are weak, which images are worn out, what would you cut? Do not rewrite it — say what is wrong.

Here are the lyrics of a song called "{title}".

{role:lyrics}

Suggest one revision that keeps the voice but fixes what is weakest. Show the changed lines only, with a sentence on why each changed.

These are the lyrics of "{title}":

{role:lyrics}

Write a short production description — genre, instruments, tempo feel, vocal treatment — that would suit them. One paragraph, concrete, no adjectives that mean nothing.

A song currently called "{title}" with these lyrics:

{role:lyrics}

Suggest six alternative titles. Take them from the text itself where you can. No explanations.

Here is “{title}”, a {kind}.

{body}

Judge it as finished work, along the axes below. Be honest rather than kind: a score that flatters is worth nothing.

